<section id="truth-model" class="global truth-model" aria-labelledby="truth-model-title">
  <h2 id="truth-model-title" tabindex="-1">Truth model / what every label means</h2>
  <div class="grid two">
    <article>
      <h3>What is directly observed</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Ranking rows and equipment recorded in this saved export.</li>
        <li>Hunter and pet events: casts, damage, activity, and detected Windfury extra-attack events.</li>
        <li>Faction when the recorded combatant or report context identifies it. Inferred faction is labeled separately.</li>
        <li>Race when a race-defining racial cast identifies it; faction alone does not identify race.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>What is deliberately NOT overclaimed</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The same-faction comparator is inside the recorded overall top five, rather than a separately fetched faction leaderboard.</li>
        <li>Zero detected Windfury procs requires trusted coverage and does not prove a totem was unavailable.</li>
        <li>Pet-family inference stays qualified; compatible abilities can leave several families possible.</li>
        <li>Projected shot targets are comparison benchmarks, not guaranteed opportunities or promised DPS.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="table-note">Calculated values use recorded data. Inferred values use a named heuristic. Unknown means the evidence cannot support an answer; it never means zero. Ranking exclusions are empirical encounter rules. Read each finding's evidence and limits.</p>
</section>
